# Ponytail & Token-Saver Rules

- Climb The Ladder before writing code: YAGNI -> Reuse existing code -> Stdlib -> Native browser/platform -> Installed dependencies -> One-line -> Minimum working code.
- Prevent over-engineering: no speculative interfaces, wrappers, or boilerplate.
- Output answers first: omit conversational filler ("Sure!", "Here is the code...").
- Keep explanations under 3 lines unless the user explicitly requested documentation.
- Never sacrifice security, accessibility, or error handling.
